  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Let's define a function P(x,y)=(x−y)2P(x, y) = (x-y)^2P(x,y)=(x−y)2. For given real numbers aaa and bbb, let's define a polynomial Qa,b(x)=P(P(P(x,a),a−b),x−b)Q_{a,b}(x) = P(P(P(x, a), a-b), x-b)Qa,b​(x)=P(P(P(x,a),a−b),x−b).\n\nNext, let's define a function F(a,b)F(a, b)F(a,b):\n\n\nIf Qa,b(x)Q_{a,b}(x)Qa,b​(x) has no real roots, F(a,b)=0F(a, b) = 0F(a,b)=0.\nOtherwise, let rrr be the largest real root of Qa,b(x)Q_{a,b}(x)Qa,b​(x).\nIf rrr is rational, it can be represented by a fraction r=pqr = \\frac{p}{q}r=qp​, where ppp and qqq are coprime integers and q&gt;0q \\gt 0q&gt;0. Then, F(a,b)=p+qF(a, b) = p + qF(a,b)=p+q.\nIf rrr is irrational, it can be proved that in this case, it can be represented in the form r=p+zqr = \\frac{p + \\sqrt{z}}{q}r=qp+z​​, where ppp, qqq and zzz are integers, q&gt;0q \\gt 0q&gt;0 and z&gt;0z \\gt 0z&gt;0. Choose the representation with the smallest value of qqq (it is guaranteed to be unique in this case). Then, F(a,b)=p+z+qF(a, b) = p + z + qF(a,b)=p+z+q.\nYou are given a sequence of integers c1,c2,…,cNc_1, c_2, \\ldots, c_Nc1​,c2​,…,cN​. Find ∑i=1N∑j=1NF(ci,cj)\\sum_{i=1}^N \\sum_{j=1}^N F(c_i, c_j)∑i=1N​∑j=1N​F(ci​,cj​).",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤201 \\leq T \\leq 201≤T≤20",
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 2 \\cdot 10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "0≤ci≤2⋅1050 \\leq c_i \\leq 2 \\cdot 10^50≤ci​≤2⋅105 for each valid iii",
      "the sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1052\\cdot 10^52⋅105",
